---
# clang-tidy config for Matcha (MatchaEngine/MatchaEditor/Sandbox/Tests).
#
# Scope: only project code is linted. HeaderFilterRegex below restricts diagnostics to headers
# under a project Code/ directory, so anything reached transitively from SDL3/EnTT/Qt6/assimp/
# nlohmann-json/spdlog/glm/imgui/efsw/pybind11 (all vcpkg-managed) is never reported on - mirrors
# what /analyze:external- already does for MSVC's own Code Analysis (see root CMakeLists.txt).
#
# To run against a specific build (needs a compile_commands.json - the "Linux Clang" CMake preset
# sets CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS, or generate one for the VS build separately):
#   clang-tidy -p Build/Clang MatchaEngine/Code/Scene/Scene.cpp
# Or via run-clang-tidy across the whole tree:
#   run-clang-tidy -p Build/Clang MatchaEngine/Code MatchaEditor/Code Sandbox/Code Tests/Code

Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,

  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '(MatchaEngine|MatchaEditor|Sandbox|Tests)[\\/]Code[\\/].*'
FormatStyle: file

# Rationale for the disables above, grouped by why - not a blanket "quiet everything" pass:
#
# Conflicts with an established, deliberate pattern in this codebase:
#   - cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes /
#     misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: ECS components (TagComponent,
#     TransformComponent, LightComponent, CameraComponent, MeshComponent, MaterialComponent, Mesh)
#     are intentionally plain public-field structs, iterated by entt views - not encapsulated
#     classes with invariants. HierarchyComponent is the deliberate exception (private fields,
#     friend-only mutation via SetParent) and correctly reports clean either way.
#   - misc-no-recursion: HierarchyComponent's CollectSubtree/DestroySubtree/DestroyEntityRecursive
#     recurse over the entity tree by design.
#   - readability-braces-around-statements: single-statement if/else bodies are written without
#     braces throughout (e.g. "if (!isRoot) continue;") - enabling this would flag nearly every
#     control-flow statement in the codebase.
#   - modernize-use-trailing-return-type: not the house style; every declaration here is
#     "ReturnType Name(...)".
#   - modernize-use-nodiscard: [[nodiscard]] is already applied by hand, deliberately (present on
#     GetComponent, absent on AddComponent, whose return value is often legitimately discarded -
#     see HierarchyComponent.h's SetParent). Auto-suggesting it everywhere a function returns
#     non-void would fight that judgment call rather than support it.
#
# Noisy for this codebase's domain (graphics/math), not indicative of a real problem:
#   - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: routine for vector/color/transform APIs
#     (SetPosition(float x, float y, float z), GL attribute binding) where same-typed adjacent
#     parameters are the whole point.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers / readability-magic-numbers: GL enums, small pixel/
#     buffer literals (e.g. Renderer's whitePixel[4]) and math constants are pervasive and
#     already-obvious in context.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays / modernize-avoid-c-arrays (two independent checks, not
#     aliases - both need disabling): small fixed-size stack buffers (whitePixel[4]) and legacy
#     C-array members (e.g. SDLInput's keyboard-state buffer) aren't worth flagging wholesale.
#   - readability-uppercase-literal-suffix: confirmed by an actual run - every float literal in
#     Vector.h/Quaternion.h/Matrix.h uses lowercase 'f' (1.0f, not 1.0F), with no exceptions found;
#     this would relitigate a settled, universal style choice on every floating-point literal in
#     the codebase.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic / -array-to-pointer-decay: GL interop code
#     works with raw buffers and pointer offsets by necessity.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg: printf-style logging (spdlog) and assimp/vararg-shaped
#     third-party APIs reached from project code trigger this without a real bug.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory: Qt widgets are parent-owned by convention (e.g.
#     `new QtViewportWidget()` handed to a layout/parent), not smart-pointer-owned - normal Qt
#     idiom, not a leak.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables: UUID.cpp's file-scope RNG state
#     (s_RandomDevice, s_Engine, s_UniformDistribution) is intentional.
#   - cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage: MT_ASSERT/MT_CORE_ERROR/MT_PROFILE_SCOPE need macros for
#     source-location capture and conditional (BUILD_PROFILING) compilation.
#   - readability-identifier-length: short math/index names (x, y, z, id) are the clearest option,
#     not a readability problem.
#   - readability-function-cognitive-complexity: a handful of functions (deserialization, shader
#     parsing) are unavoidably branchy; worth tuning a threshold for deliberately later rather than
#     guessing one now.
#   - misc-include-cleaner: this project pulls from ten-plus vcpkg packages with deep transitive
#     includes; strict include-what-you-use hygiene is a separate, opt-in effort, not a default-on
#     lint.
#   - portability-avoid-pragma-once: every header in this codebase opens with "#pragma once" (not
#     traditional include guards) - confirmed by an actual run, which flagged it on every header it
#     touched. Universally supported by the three compilers this project already targets
#     (MSVC, Clang, GCC), so there's no real portability gap being flagged here.

CheckOptions:
  # Naming mirrors what's already consistently used across the codebase - this section describes
  # the existing convention, it doesn't introduce a new one.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase
    value: CamelCase
  # "detail" (HierarchyComponent.h's implementation-only namespace) follows the near-universal
  # C++ idiom of a lowercase nested namespace for "not part of the public API" - not a name this
  # codebase chose to violate its own convention with.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^(detail|internal)$'
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.StructCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.TemplateParameterCase
    value: CamelCase

  - key: readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.FunctionIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^main$'

  - key: readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase
    value: CamelCase
  # Overrides of Qt virtuals (QWidget/QObject event handlers) keep Qt's own lowerCamelCase names -
  # e.g. SceneHierarchyWidget::dropEvent/mousePressEvent/keyPressEvent/focusOutEvent. These aren't
  # names this codebase chose; they're required to match the base class signature being overridden.
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.MethodIgnoredRegexp
    value: '^(mouse|key|drag|drop|focus|paint|resize|close|wheel|show|hide|context)[A-Za-z]*Event$|^event$|^eventFilter$|^event$'

  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase
    value: camelBack
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ParameterPackCase
    value: camelBack
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.LocalVariableCase
    value: camelBack

  # Private/protected data members: m_PascalCase (m_RendererAPI, m_ChangeBatchDepth, ...).
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberPrefix
    value: m_
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberPrefix
    value: m_

  # Public data members: plain camelBack, no prefix - the deliberate signal that these are
  # ECS-component-style plain data (MeshComponent::mesh, HierarchyComponent's own GetChildrenCount
  # etc. return these), not implementation state (see the non-private-member-variables disable
  # above for why that's intentional here rather than an oversight).
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberCase
    value: camelBack

  # File-scope/class-static state: s_PascalCase (UUID.cpp's s_RandomDevice/s_Engine/
  # s_UniformDistribution; the removed RendererAPI::s_ActiveRendererAPI followed the same pattern).
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.StaticVariableCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.StaticVariablePrefix
    value: s_
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.GlobalVariableCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.GlobalVariablePrefix
    value: s_

  # Deliberately left unconstrained: compile-time constants are named two different ways in the
  # existing code (Renderer.h's "MAX_LIGHTS" all-caps vs. Renderer.cpp's "kLightArrayOffset")
  # with no single rule to describe both without flagging one of them as wrong. Pick one and
  # enable ConstexprVariableCase/GlobalConstantCase/StaticConstantCase once the team settles on a
  # single style, rather than have this file silently declare a winner.

  - key: readability-redundant-member-init.IgnoreBaseInCopyConstructors
    value: 'true'
  - key: modernize-loop-convert.UseCxx20ReverseRanges
    value: 'true'
  - key: performance-move-const-arg.CheckTriviallyCopyableMove
    value: 'true'
